A black-box prediction slows down coders because they must still read the entire 5-page chart to verify the AI's claims. The model is trained to output structured JSON pairing each code with its exact supporting evidence:

```json
{
  "diagnoses": [
    {
      "code": "E11.65",
      "description": "Type 2 diabetes mellitus with hyperglycemia",
      "evidence": "Patient presents with uncontrolled blood glucose at 285 mg/dL; longstanding T2D.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "procedures": [
    {
      "code": "99214",
      "modifier": "25",
      "description": "Office visit, established patient, level 4",
      "evidence": "Comprehensive 35-minute consultation addressing multiple uncontrolled chronic conditions alongside joint injection.",
      "confidence": 0.94
    }
  ]
}
```
In the Epic UI, clicking a suggested code highlights the supporting sentence directly in the doctor's note, allowing the coder to verify accuracy in seconds.
